9. FINDINGS
  ........................................................
  F1  BLOCKING. tools/verify-tone.py has no test; P3 is MISSED. The oracle is
      correct today (section 3), but nothing in the repository would notice if it
      stopped being able to fail. Remedy: commit the section-3 battery as a
      stdlib-only test (synthesised WAVs: 440 pass, 880/220 fail, silence fails,
      1328 samples fail, unfinalized 440 passes). A2's file.
  F2  Check 6 measures the return value of the function that computes it; it can
      fail but cannot prove LPIB moved. Suggest asserting on stream_lpib() across
      a known interval, or comparing cycles against WAV duration.
  F3  a3dd44f writes 0x3C to SDnSTS and the comment names three flags (BCIS=0x04,
      DESE=0x10, FIFOE=0x20 = 0x34). 0x3C also sets bit 3 (0x08), which the
      comment does not name. Writing a reserved bit is ignored by the hardware, so
      this is a comment/mask mismatch, not a fault.
  F4  Audio verification is keyed on exit code 33 in two places (see section 7).
  F5  a3dd44f's message says "10/10 ... 20/20"; the linked run printed 11 and 22.
  F6  docs/logs/k5-hda-output.log prints the guest's 48 kHz and the WAV's 44100 Hz
      without saying QEMU resamples; it reads like a contradiction.
  F7  Observation for F1.11 (not my item): both of my plant branches' `repro` runs
      failed with `DIFFER: kernel ELF binary hashes mismatch across Linux and
      Windows` (42265842709 at 49 s, 42265860068 at 58 s), while a3dd44f's own
      repro run (42265173885) succeeded minutes earlier. A one-constant change
      cannot explain host divergence, so the C5 gate looks flaky. Handed to F1.11.
      It also means the check.yml `repro` workflow is red on my plant branches for
      a reason unrelated to the plant.

